# Enkaku — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so never put a real
# secret here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# HOW IT IS LOADED, AND THE ONE PLACE IT IS NOT
# ---------------------------------------------
# Bun loads this file automatically for anything it *runs as code* — the core, the cloud
# node, and every script under `scripts/`. Nothing else is needed: no dotenv package, no
# import.
#
# It is NOT expanded inside `package.json` script strings. `bun run dev:studio` resolves
# `${NEXT_PUBLIC_ENKAKU_CORE_URL:-...}` in a shell that never saw this file, so a value set
# here would be silently ignored there. Studio's own variables therefore live in
# `packages/studio/.env` (Next.js loads that one itself) — see `packages/studio/.env.example`.
#
# Precedence is env > file > default (spec §5). A real shell variable always wins over this
# file, which is what makes one-off overrides work:
#
#   ENKAKU_LOG_LEVEL=debug bun run dev
#
# Everything here is optional. Plain `bun run dev` works with this file absent entirely.


# ── Core ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the database, tools, artifacts and logs live. The dev scripts already point at
# .dev-data/ .dev-cloud/ .dev-node/, so set this only to override that.
# ENKAKU_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/enkaku

# ENKAKU_PORT=7700
# ENKAKU_BIND=127.0.0.1          # non-loopback ⇒ server auth mode ⇒ TLS required
# ENKAKU_CONFIG=<dataDir>/enkaku.config.json
# ENKAKU_MODE=orchestrator       # cloud control plane; never touches local adb
# ENKAKU_LOG_LEVEL=info          # debug | info | warn | error
# ENKAKU_LOG_JSON=1              # JSON-lines output, for shipping to a log collector
# ENKAKU_STUDIO_DIST=<cwd>/packages/studio/out

# Open a browser at boot. OFF by default — starting a server should not take
# over your screen, and a developer restarting the core loses focus every time.
# Set this to opt in. The headless guards still apply on top of it: never in
# orchestrator mode, never on a non-loopback bind, never without a TTY.
# ENKAKU_OPEN=1


# ── Auth and TLS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auth mode is derived from the bind address unless forced here. A non-loopback bind in
# `local` mode fails the boot rather than silently exposing an unauthenticated farm.
# ENKAKU_AUTH_MODE=auto          # auto | local | server
# ENKAKU_TLS_MODE=off            # off | self | external
# `self` with NO cert/key below: the core generates and renews its own
# certificate under <dataDir>/tls/ and loads it on every later start. Enough
# for a farm on a trusted LAN; browsers still warn, because self-signed
# proves no identity. Set both paths to bring your own instead.
# ENKAKU_TLS_CERT=/path/fullchain.pem
# ENKAKU_TLS_KEY=/path/privkey.pem
# ENKAKU_ALLOW_INSECURE=1        # server mode without TLS. Testing only; it warns loudly.
# ENKAKU_PUBLISH_TOKEN=          # require a token on POST /api/scripts

# The login rate limiter (and the `sessions.ip` audit column) key on the real socket peer
# address by default — it cannot be spoofed. Only set this when the core sits behind a
# reverse proxy YOU control (the `ENKAKU_TLS_MODE=external` Caddy/nginx path above): it then
# trusts `X-Forwarded-For`, taking the rightmost hop (the one the proxy itself appended), never
# the leftmost, client-controlled one. Turning this on with no real proxy in front lets any
# direct caller spoof the header and evade the lockout entirely — leave it unset unless you
# know you need it.
# ENKAKU_TRUST_PROXY=1


# ── Device network route (the proxy feature) ───────────────────────────────────
# Without a probe endpoint the `egress`, `geo` and `dns` checks stay `skip` and a route's
# health can never rise above `unverified` — applied, but never confirmed to be carrying
# traffic. That is deliberate: an unproven route must never report itself healthy.
#
# Any endpoint that echoes the caller's address works for the `egress` check. Real DNS-leak
# detection needs one you host yourself, because it has to observe which resolver actually
# looked up the name — see docs/archive/plans/51-m24b-verified-egress-and-fail-closed.md §3.3.
# ENKAKU_NETWORK_PROBE_URL=https://api.ipify.org/?format=json

# The zone `packages/probe-server` is authoritative for, once your DNS provider delegates it
# (see that package's README). Only this makes the `dns` check real: the core mints a one-time
# nonce subdomain, the device asks for it through the tunnel, and the probe server reports which
# resolver actually looked it up. Unset → `dns` stays `skip`. Cannot work against localhost —
# the query has to arrive from the public internet.
# ENKAKU_NETWORK_PROBE_DNS_ZONE=dns.probe.example.com

# The `geo` check's IP→location lookup is NOT an env var — it is a farm setting,
# `network.geoProvider`, set in Studio under Settings → Network, because it is the kind of thing
# an operator changes without restarting the core. Point it at `packages/probe-server`'s `/geo`.
# Unlike the probe URL above, this one is called by the CORE, not by the device, so a
# `http://127.0.0.1:8080/geo` running on the same machine is perfectly valid.

# Sticky-session template for the upstream username, so a device keeps the same exit address
# across reconnects. Provider-specific — SOAX and others each spell it differently — so it is
# a template rather than a hardcoded format. `{id}` is the device's stable session id.
# Leave unset for no stickiness.
# ENKAKU_NETWORK_SESSION_TEMPLATE={username}-sessionid-{id}


# ── AI agents — provider connector credentials ──────────────────────────────────
# A stored connector credential (Settings → Connectors) always wins. Either of these is only
# a fallback for a connector left with no credential of its own (plan 65 §3.6, plan 75 §4.4) —
# useful for a single-operator dev setup where creating a connector record feels like ceremony.
# ENKAKU_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ENKAKU_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=


# ── Guest agent (the on-device APK) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Resolution order: this variable, then a local Gradle build under apps/guest-agent/, then
# the sha256-pinned artifact from the Toolchain Manager. Set this only to pin a one-off
# build; a checkout that has run `bun run build:guest-agent` needs nothing.
# ENKAKU_GUEST_AGENT_PATH=$PWD/apps/guest-agent/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk


# ── Cloud mode ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_CP_URL=http://localhost:7700    # control plane, required for the node
# ENKAKU_ENROLL_TOKEN=                   # one-time, first run only; discarded afterwards
# ENKAKU_NODE_NAME=
# ENKAKU_PUBLIC_URL=


# ── Job heartbeat and scheduler ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_JOB_HEARTBEAT_TTL=60
# ENKAKU_JOB_HEARTBEAT_MS=15000
# ENKAKU_JOB_REAPER_MS=5000
# ENKAKU_SCHEDULER_INTERVAL_MS=2000


# ── Job isolation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Crash containment, not a security sandbox — never describe it as one (spec §11.3).
# ENKAKU_JOB_ISOLATION=process   # process | container
# ENKAKU_JOB_IMAGE=oven/bun:1
# ENKAKU_JOB_CPUS=
# ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_MB=
# ENKAKU_OCI_RUNTIME=            # e.g. runsc for gVisor
# ENKAKU_CONTAINER_RUNTIME=


# ── Toolchain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_TOOLS_MANIFEST_URL=
# ENKAKU_UI_SERVER_PORT_RANGE=27100-27299
# ENKAKU_REVERSE_DEVICE_PORT_RANGE=28100-28299
                                 # Ports ON THE PHONE for `adb reverse` (plan 114 §4.3), not on this
                                 # machine — a different namespace from the range above, deliberately
                                 # numbered next to it. Kept below Android's ephemeral floor (32768)
                                 # so a transient outbound socket cannot already hold the port.
# ENKAKU_ADB_PATH=               # dev/test only; logs a warning whenever it is used.
                                 # The generic form is ENKAKU_<TOOL_ID>_PATH.


# ── Support overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Values that used to be settings and are now constants (docs/plans/212-mvp-settings.md).
# None of these appears in Studio. Set one only when support asks you to; an invalid value
# fails the boot with E_BAD_CONFIG rather than falling back. `none` means "unset" for the
# three that accept it (ENKAKU_JOB_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS, ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_MAX_BYTES,
# ENKAKU_GEO_PROVIDER_URL).
# ENKAKU_TOUCH_PROFILES=                        # JSON, the three profiles' tuples
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_SCREEN_OFF_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_OFFLINE_GRACE_SEC=20
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_RECOVERY_COOLDOWN_SEC=120
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_RECOVERY_PROBE_INTERVAL_SEC=60
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_ENDPOINTS_REMEMBERED=4
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_ENDPOINT_RETIRE_AFTER=10
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_CONNECT_SETTLE_MS=3000
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_RESCAN_INTERVAL_SEC=10
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_AUTO_QUARANTINE=true
# ENKAKU_BATTERY_POLL_INTERVAL_SEC=60
# ENKAKU_DEVICE_LABEL_SURFACE=lock-screen        # lock-screen | wallpaper
# ENKAKU_LABEL_WRITE_CONCURRENCY=2
# ENKAKU_CONTROL_IDLE_SEC=30
# ENKAKU_ADB_TCP_PORT=5555
# ENKAKU_ADB_MAX_STREAMS_PER_DEVICE=4
# ENKAKU_ADB_MAX_STREAMS_FARM=0
# ENKAKU_ADB_MAX_HOST_PROCESSES=4
# ENKAKU_ADB_TIMEOUT_STORM_RATE=0.5
# ENKAKU_ADB_RESTART_COOLDOWN_SEC=60
# ENKAKU_ADB_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# ENKAKU_SCAN_MODE=on-demand                     # off | on-demand
# ENKAKU_SCAN_MAX_ADDRESSES=1024
# ENKAKU_SCAN_CONCURRENCY=32
# ENKAKU_SCAN_PROBE_TIMEOUT_MS=300
# ENKAKU_CUTOVER_WINDOW_SEC=180
# ENKAKU_CUTOVER_POLL_SEC=5
# ENKAKU_GUEST_AGENT_PROVISION=auto              # auto | manual | off
# ENKAKU_GUEST_AGENT_RECOVERY_REARM_SEC=120
# ENKAKU_CRASH_WATCH=always                      # always | off
# ENKAKU_JOB_RESET_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# ENKAKU_JOB_RESET_STRICT=false
# ENKAKU_JOB_STARTUP_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# ENKAKU_JOB_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS=none
# ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_MAX_BYTES=none
# ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_ENFORCE=kill                 # kill | warn | off
# ENKAKU_JOB_MEMORY_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_MS=2000
# ENKAKU_JOB_TRIGGER_MAX_DEPTH=5
# ENKAKU_JOB_TRIGGER_MAX_PER_CHAIN=200
# ENKAKU_JOB_TRIGGER_MAX_PER_JOB=10
# ENKAKU_JOB_MAX_RESULT_BYTES=65536
# ENKAKU_JOB_PROGRESS_INTERVAL_MS=1000
# ENKAKU_JOB_RETRY_BACKOFF_MAX_MS=30000
# ENKAKU_JOB_TIMEOUT_IS_INFRA=false
# ENKAKU_JOB_REBIND_ON_INFRA=true
# ENKAKU_JOB_CRASH_POLICY=declared               # ignore | declared | any
# ENKAKU_WORKFLOW_MAX_TOTAL_MS=21600000
# ENKAKU_INPUT_EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS=3
# ENKAKU_EVENT_MAX_ROWS_PER_DEVICE=50000
# ENKAKU_BLOB_ORPHAN_GRACE_HOURS=24
# ENKAKU_AUDIT_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# A simulated run (trigger: 'simulate') is scratch work, not history: pruned on
# its own short horizon, independent of storage.historyDays. 1-30.
# ENKAKU_SIMULATE_RUN_RETENTION_DAYS=2
# ENKAKU_SHELL_EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# ENKAKU_SHELL_MAX_OUTPUT_BYTES=262144
# ENKAKU_ADB_ENDPOINT_ENABLED=false
# ENKAKU_ADB_ENDPOINT_BIND=127.0.0.1
# ENKAKU_ADB_ENDPOINT_IDLE_SEC=300
# ENKAKU_ADB_ENDPOINT_MAX_STREAMS=8
# ENKAKU_INPUT_WAIT_BUDGET_MS=5000
# ENKAKU_INPUT_MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH=32
# ENKAKU_DISPLAY_FALLBACK_RETRIES=6
# ENKAKU_WALL_MAX_TILES=0
# ENKAKU_WALL_RAMP_CONCURRENCY=2
# ENKAKU_WALL_DECODE_TILE_CEILING=24
# ENKAKU_WALL_LAN_BANDWIDTH_BPS=200000000
# ENKAKU_WALL_TRANSPORT_OVERRIDE=auto            # auto | loopback | lan | wan
# ENKAKU_READINESS_MAX_HOT=8
# ENKAKU_READINESS_DEFAULT_DESIRED=awake         # asleep | awake | hot
# ENKAKU_TRANSFER_ENABLED=true
# ENKAKU_WORKSPACE_MAX_FILE_BYTES=268435456
# ENKAKU_WORKSPACE_MAX_FILES_PER_SCOPE=1000
# ENKAKU_WORKSPACE_MAX_BYTES_PER_SCOPE=8589934592
# ENKAKU_WORKSPACE_INLINE_MAX_BYTES=65536
# ENKAKU_KV_MAX_VALUE_BYTES=65536
# ENKAKU_KV_MAX_KEY_LENGTH=256
# ENKAKU_KV_MAX_ENTRIES_PER_NAMESPACE=1000
# ENKAKU_KV_MAX_ENTRIES_PER_DEVICE=5000
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_ANCHOR_QUIET_MS=400
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_ANCHOR_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=1500
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_LONG_PRESS_MS=400
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_MAX_STEPS=500
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_MAX_DURATION_SEC=900
# ENKAKU_RECORDING_CAPTURE_SCREENSHOTS=true
# ENKAKU_GEO_PROVIDER_URL=none
# ENKAKU_GEO_RECHECK_INTERVAL_SEC=300


# ── SDK / CLI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ENKAKU_FARM_URL=http://localhost:7700
# ENKAKU_TOKEN=


# ── Tests ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests needing a physical device are skipped unless this is set, so `bun test` stays green
# with nothing plugged in.
# ENKAKU_TEST_DEVICE=1

# Upstream for the guest-agent smoke test. Without it the route stages skip rather than fail.
# Use a scratch credential — never a production one.
# ENKAKU_SMOKE_PROXY=socks5://user:pass@host:1080


# ── Support overrides ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plan 206 §3.5 — the always-on builder's farm-wide ceiling on concurrent session
# builds, across every USB root combined (the per-root knob is a farm setting,
# `session.buildsPerUsbRoot`). Not meant to be tuned casually; raise it only under
# support guidance for a farm whose real USB topology needs it.
# ENKAKU_SESSION_BUILD_CEILING=16
